From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:57:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio: J604: match the J616s config
 again, not the J614s

Aurora 7.3 (dae5290dc5 "ASoC: apple: macaudio: add the J604 and the M4
iMacs") added "apple,j604-macaudio" -> macaudio_j614_cfg, which has
enable_speakers = false and never binds the speaker link. The J604
series' own entry from 1.617 ("apple,j604-macaudio" -> macaudio_j616_cfg,
under which the J604 speakers were brought up with speakersafetyd) was
carried into the 7.3 integration below Aurora's, and the OF match takes
the first entry. So on 7.3 the J604 binds the J614s config:

  snd-soc-macaudio sound: driver can't assure safety on this model,
  disabling speakers

With no speaker link, the six SN012776 amps register no controls, so
speakersafetyd cannot lock "Left Woofer 1 VSENSE Switch" (ENOENT) and
crash-loops to start-limit-hit.

Keep one J604 entry, the J616s config, as on 1.617. Protection is
unchanged: the speaker link still needs the boot loader's amp levels
(macaudio_sn012776_levels_present()), and "Speaker Volume Unlock"
(speakersafetyd) stays the default interface at every bind.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 9 +++------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index d62208a9e9..7bb19ccce3 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -4067,8 +4067,9 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j616_cfg = {
  * J614s: the same amps and frame as the J616s, but its speakers have not
  * been brought up and have no protection profile. Keep them off entirely
  * until they get their own bring-up: the speaker link is not bound, so no
- * stream ever reaches the amps. The J604 (T8132, MacBook Pro 14" M4) has
- * the same amps, frame and chassis, and is in the same state.
+ * stream ever reaches the amps. (The J604, T8132 MacBook Pro 14" M4, has
+ * the same amps and frame and has been brought up: it takes the J616s
+ * configuration, under speakersafetyd.)
  */
 struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j614_cfg = {
 	.enable_speakers = false,
@@ -4225,10 +4226,6 @@ static const struct of_device_id macaudio_snd_device_id[]  = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j575c-macaudio-jack", .data = &macaudio_j616_jack_cfg },
 	/* j613    AID20   sn012776    15      2x 1W+1T Compat: apple,j413-macaudio */
 	/* j615    AID21   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T Compat: apple,j415-macaudio */
-	/* j604    -       sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed; speakers off until bring-up) */
-	{ .compatible = "apple,j604-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j614_cfg },
-	/* j604    -       cs42l84     -       the jack, a card of its own (AOP-fed) */
-	{ .compatible = "apple,j604-macaudio-jack", .data = &macaudio_j616_jack_cfg },
 	/* j604    AID30   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed, the J616s layout) */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j604-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j616_cfg },
 	/* j604    AID30   cs42l84     -       the jack, a card of its own (AOP-fed) */
